  "energy_arc": "Mukhada ignites at high energy (8/10) with sitar and full rhythm section locked in groove.\nGuitar takeover increases physical aggression (9/10) with relentless thrash chugging and kick syncopation.\nTaan long pushes the peak (10/10) through blazing sitar runs and soaring upper-register bends.\nReturning mukhada hits maximum climactic impact (10/10) before snapping shut on the final hard stop.",
  "rhythm_section": {
    "reasoning": "Plan: Bhairav thrash groove at 180 bpm in Teentaal (16 beats). For Section 0 (mukhada), lock into the chord plan S power 8 | r power 4 | d power 2 | S power 2. The guitar provides driving palm-muted thrash gallops on low S roots, then shifts up a half-step grind to r for 4 beats, drops to d for 2 beats, and finishes on a heavy unison punch on S leading to the sam. Section 1 (takeover) is handled by code from the realised head, so no part is written for it. Section 2 (taan_long) drives full tilt underneath the blazing chaugun solo, maintaining relentless rhythmic gallops primarily pedaled on S, driving the climax feel with high-energy push. Section 3 (final mukhada) recalls the primary pattern of Section 0 using same_as to slam shut on the final sam.",
